    "input_tokens": 2847,
    "output_tokens": 134
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 2,
   "response_text": "This is very interesting! The validation accuracy is approximately 0.963 (ranging from 0.959 to 0.966), which is **significantly higher** than the healthy range of 0.8519\u20130.8607. This is a clear anomaly. The training loss shows normal decreasing behavior, but the validation accuracy is abnormally high.\n\nLet me check the training code and logs to understand what might be causing this:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_017V8ry4RR2qFNPcesciN5vW",
     "name": "read_code",
     "arguments": {
